/*
  GameKit shows these keys to the other player as notification text whenever an
  exchange is sent (XCHG_UPDATE) or answered (XCHG_REPLY) -- see
  CodeaTurnBasedMatches.lua sendExchangeWithDataTable. An empty value does NOT
  hide the banner: iOS treats it as a missing entry and shows the raw key
  (confirmed on device 2026-10-31). So both need real wording.

  XCHG_UPDATE is the only one the app sends now: the non-holder's finished round
  (score + comment together). The app no longer replies to exchanges, so
  XCHG_REPLY only matters for exchanges answered by older builds.
*/
"XCHG_UPDATE" = "Your opponent has finished their round.";
"XCHG_REPLY" = "Your opponent has seen your update.";
